/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Let the message m(t) occupy fL to W hertz.
   - BDSB = 2W, BSSB = W, BVSB = W + fv
   - W is the highest message frequency in hertz and fv the width of the vestige in hertz.
   - For one test tone, AM at m = 1 radiates 1.5Pc, DSB-SC radiates the two sidebands, 0.5Pc, and SSB one sideband, 0.25Pc.
   - Filter method.
   - Phase-shift (Hartley) method.
   - sUSB(t) = m(t) cos 2πfct − m̂(t) sin 2πfct
   - the upper sideband; a plus sign gives the lower sideband.
   - For a tone, cos 2πfmt cos 2πfct − sin 2πfmt sin 2πfct = cos 2π(fc + fm)t, one line at fc + fm.
   - Weaver (third) method.
*/
