/* book Worked example 2: Q: A VSB filter has gain rising in a straight line from 0 at fc − 0.75 MHz to 1 at fc + 0.75 MHz. Find its gain at fc, fc ± 0.25 MHz and fc ± 0.5 MHz, and check the VSB condition.
   1. The line is H(fc + x) = 0.5 + x/(2 × 0.75) for |x| ≤ 0.75 MHz.
   2. x = 0: H = 0.5.
   3. x = +0.25: 0.5 + 0.167 = 0.667; x = −0.25: 0.5 − 0.167 = 0.333. Sum 1.000.
   4. x = +0.5: 0.5 + 0.333 = 0.833; x = −0.5: 0.167. Sum 1.000.
   5. Every pair adds to 1, so the folded vestige fills in exactly what the upper sideband lost near fc.
   Answer: H = 0.5 at fc; 0.667 and 0.333 at ±0.25 MHz; 0.833 and 0.167 at ±0.5 MHz. Each pair sums to 1, so the filter meets the VSB condition. */
