/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Near its bias point the current i of a nonlinear device can be written as a power series in its input voltage v.
   - i = a0 + a1v + a2v²
   - i in mA, v in volts; a0 is the bias current (mA), a1 the slope (mA/V) and a2 the square-law coefficient (mA/V²).
   - Apply v = Ac cos ωct + Am cos ωmt, where ω = 2πf.
   - Only the cross product makes sidebands.
   - Carrier and message are added and applied to the device.
   - m = 2a2Am / a1
   - m is the modulation index.
   - The filter must reject DC, the message at fm and its harmonic at 2fm, and the harmonic at 2fc.
   - Two matched square-law devices receive the same carrier but opposite message: v1 = c(t) + m(t) and v2 = c(t) − m(t), with c(t) = Ac cos ωct.
*/
